                                                    "text": "prepend preset"
                                                }
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "box": {
                                                    "format": 6,
                                                    "id": "obj-6",
                                                    "maxclass": "flonum",
                                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                                    "numoutlets": 2,
                                                    "outlettype": [ "", "bang" ],
                                                    "parameter_enable": 0,
                                                    "patching_rect": [ 336.0, 210.0, 50.0, 22.0 ]
                                                }
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "box": {
                                                    "id": "obj-7",
                                                    "linecount": 4,
                                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                                    "patching_rect": [ 336.0, 135.0, 173.0, 60.0 ],
                                                    "text": "you can change preset from outside by sending in the first inlet the preset number (int or float) with a prepend \"preset\" "
                                                }
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "box": {
                                                    "id": "obj-3",
                                                    "linecount": 41,
                                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                                    "patching_rect": [ 6.0, 44.0, 315.0, 556.0 ],
                                                    "text": "3 low frequency oscillator floats (bipolar) to be used for modulation of floats or 3d motion: position / rotation / scale\n\nget the 3 singular modulated floats from out 1, 2, and 3\nout 4 5 6 give bangs at X, Y, Z loop start\n\nplug the 7th out in the 1st in of a [ste.3dModel] and select the desired outMode\n\noutFrequency: is the frequency of output, if you are using it for visuals, with a 3dWorld keep it as synced with ste.3dWorld\n\nout7Mode: when plugged in a 3dModel or a 3dPointLight etc from the 1st outlet to 1st inlet, it decides what the 3 oscillators are animating (position, rotatexyz, scale)\n\nfor each oscillator you can:\nturn ON or OFF, frequency (speed), amplitude, center (around which number is the oscillation centered) mode (oscillator shape), phase (at which point of the shape is the oscillator starting) sync (reset oscillation at start) init (initialize parameters)\n\nrange mode gives you the possiblity to decide how you want to define the oscillators' range: with min and max or with amplitude and center\n\nas the oscillators are bipolar the values of amp 1 and center 0 generates an oscillation between -0.5 0.5 this makes sense when moving things around in 3d\n\nthere is a syncAll button to restart all oscillators together\n\nthis can be useful for example when switching between range modes and resetting the min max or the amp center, the values will suddenly jump\nthis only happens once because of the mode switch and will not happen again (unless you change rangeMode again)"
                                                }
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "box": {
                                                    "comment": "",
                                                    "id": "obj-1",
                                                    "index": 1,
                                                    "maxclass": "inlet",
